cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HLCtools, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "HLCtools: Calculate Herd Lying Concordance Metrics"
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amorim Franchi"
    given-names: "Guilherme"
    email: "gaf@anivet.au.dk"
    affiliation: "Aarhus University"
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7653-6512
abstract: "HLCtools calculates Herd Lying Concordance metrics from individual animal lying-behaviour data. Herd Lying Concordance is a framework for quantifying group-level behavioural cohesion from the distribution of individual lying behaviour within observation intervals. The package supports multiple dispersion-based implementations, threshold synchrony comparisons, lying-weighted extensions, daily summaries, and descriptive method-ranking tools."
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - animal welfare
  - dairy cattle
  - lying behaviour
  - synchrony
  - group cohesion
  - precision livestock farming
  - accelerometer
